%decision SaleMutationHandlersRemoved
  what:    saleServer serves only list, get, void and refund; the create / add item / remove item / add payment / remove payment / finalize / clear handlers were deleted
  why:     They accepted client-built money and the old finalize had no payment check. withComplianceLog, requireAuth and showT are imported by Server.SaleCommand.
  affects: saleServer, withComplianceLog, requireAuth

%decision IdentityComesFromTheSession
  what:    The employee recorded on a sale, on a register open and on a register close is the signed-in user; no request body names an employee
  why:     Before 2026-10-06 the browser chose the employee, so any login could record a sale under anyone. The employee id fields left StartSaleRequest, OpenRegisterRequest and CloseRegisterRequest on 2026-10-10. The handlers pass the session user's id to Service.Sale.startSale, Service.Register.openRegister and closeRegister as an argument. A client that still sends the old field is accepted and the field is ignored, because Aeson's generic decoder skips unknown keys. nix/sale-checks/identity.sh checks this.
  affects: registerServer, requireAuth

%decision SaleOwnershipAndCapabilities
  what:    A write to an existing sale needs the right capability and needs the caller to be the employee who opened the sale, a Manager or an Admin
  why:     Owner decision 2026-10-06: start rigid; sharing a sale between employees can be added to the specification later. Cashiers must not void. Sale commands need capCanProcessTransaction. Void needs capCanVoidTransaction, refund capCanRefundTransaction, register open and close capCanOpenRegister and capCanCloseRegister. requireSaleWriter reads the sale's employee BEFORE the command takes the row lock. That is safe only because no command changes the employee after the sale is opened. A command that reassigns a sale would have to move this check under the lock. Void and refund check the capability but NOT ownership: anyone with the capability may void or refund any sale.
  affects: requireCapability, mayWriteSale, requireSaleWriter, saleServer

%decision RegisterCreateAndUpdateNeedManageRegisters
  what:    POST /register and PUT /register/:id require capCanManageRegisters
  why:     Owner decision 2026-10-08: only a manager or admin may create a register. Built 2026-10-10, after the frontend stopped creating registers on the fly. A cashier gets 403 and no row is written. nix/sale-checks/identity.sh checks both.
  affects: registerServer


